ecause when we've seen him as  Patrick Stewart who's always been  fantastic but he's just he's just very  stoic he's very wise he's he's got  everything together when we saw him in  first class he wasn't quite there yet  but you saw pretty through line to where  he was gonna be but now we see this he  had this middle ground where he just  completely dropped the bottom fell out  and his life was a mess and that just  adds a lot of dimension to him I really  had a lot of fun with the contrast of  magneto in terms of how he is in this  film and how we see him in the future  when he's like look all that stuff  didn't matter we just need to be  together and deal with this and just to  see the lengths that he was willing to  go to back in the 70s it's a fantastic  contrast and its really well-balanced  I'm not going to go through this element  by element but the effects are fantastic  the cast is fantastic a lot of the  characters that could have been  throwaways they're given performances  and just enough tiny little beats that  it works really well Quicksilver  completely steals the show and the other  thing that I really like is that this  one by the end feels very much like a  closure feels like a closed chapter  obviously we've got a post-credits scene  that sets up apocalypse which I'm  nervous about but I talked about that at  the round table but I really do love the  fact that this feels very much like the  closing of a book there's more that can  be told especially with the younger  versions of the cast but I like the  feeling of closure that this film has  and it's it's something nice and that it  doesn't be in it's something it doesn't  feel like we're getting a lot in comic  book movies anymore so that's another  added bonus for this thing for me as  well I'm not sure where it lands for me  in terms of overall ranking I think it  might be just barely behind first class  for me that's a really tight race though  x 2 is still my personal favorite but  it's it's 